| Dependencies and scope | `C-LINEAR-NONMATCH` supplies the canonical simple triangle-free train-crossing graph and its strict-rhombus direction separation. The finite theorem is conditional on the explicit actual force-hull annulus; it assumes no annulus rate and proves no motion. All source points, including contact isolates, remain retained. The pentagon regression is finite, local, and nonglobal; it is compatible with `C-FULL-FLOWER-PROJECTIVE-BLOCKER`, which allows five terminals. |
| Counterexamples and corrections checked | The exact verifier checks every pair in six fixtures, contact graphs, face walks, hull support, train decomposition, selected ends, the exact finite identities, and Mantel checks. The pentagonal flower has 15 core points, 20 unit contacts, five square faces, one central pentagon, ten extreme vertices, and five unit hull sides. It does not show source-vertex-disjoint trains, global capacity failure, global optimality, or Level I failure. The source's product-measure proof is not imported. |
