| Exact claim audited | Section 4 claims that for owner set I with loaded-hull run counts r_i and unary-rhombus-root owner set J, the overlap-aware sum of run costs and roots outside I is at most the selected O-O train count. |
| Independent reconstruction | Exact mixed squared-norm identity forbids an old contact between distinct mutually acute moving owners. A nonzero selected cut therefore separates zero from one owner when its region labels are constant. For pairwise disjoint proper cuts, this gives disjoint owner banks T_i. Each loaded-hull run maps to two distinct outer terminal occurrences in its own bank, while each rhombus-only root has its opposite moving/fixed contacts in one train of its root owner's bank. Summing disjoint owner banks proves sum_{i in I} r_i + |J minus I| <= T_OO. |
| Dependencies and scope | C-OO-LOWER-BLOCKER-LOCALIZATION, C-ACUTE-BINARY-OO-LAMINARITY, C-OWNER-REGION-TREE-RECURRENCE, C-NEAR-UNIT-CONFLICT-GEOMETRY, and C-LINEAR-NONMATCH. Pairwise disjoint proper crosscuts and a nonempty outer-walk complement for I are explicit hypotheses. Arbitrary crossing multishears, unloaded tails, contact-isolate endpoints, full-source feasibility, and global optimality are not included. |
| Counterexamples and corrections checked | Repeated labels on disconnected regions do not collide because each zero/owner cut has one label bank. Singleton bridges retain two distinct facial occurrences. I intersect J is charged once through r_i. The source verifier's abstract one-train unary packet has no source realization and does not refute this theorem. |
| Verdict and canonical disposition | PASS WITH NARROWED SCOPE — promote C-OO-OVERLAP-AWARE-ROOT-RUN-CAPACITY. The theorem closes Audit.63's owner-bank allocation gap only in the stated pairwise-disjoint acute-binary cut system. |
| Verification | Reran the frozen source verifier: 14,182 abstract tree-bank checks, 110,887 Horn/pinning checks, and 72 binary packets passed. Those computations do not verify outer-run injection or rhombus support; these are proved analytically in the audit. The 22 theorem-state tooling tests, state/route checks, generated views, and whitespace check passed locally; all 75 unique registered certificates passed. PR-aware validation, protected CI, and post-merge workflow are pending. |
